<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1661–1706</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville was a soldier and explorer born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>. He raided English posts on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a> and in 1696-1697 destroyed most English settlements on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> from Plaisance. In 1699 he built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-maurepas">Fort Maurepas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biloxi">Biloxi</a>, beginning the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-le-moyne-diberville.jpg" alt="Pierre Le Moyne d'Iberville" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait,_Pierre_Le_Moyne_d%27Iberville,_Montr%C3%A9al_Archives.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
